Error: Jet.FailureDomainNotErrorType: Explicit failure domain `[Plain]` is not an Error type
  --> Tests/UI/ErrorConversions/list_of_plain_values_is_no_failure_domain.jet:7:22
    |
  7 | check: fn(x: Int) -> Int [Plain]! {
    |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A `!` contract may name `Err`, a Core error, a type marked `#Error`, an all-error union, or `Never`; arbitrary value types do not describe failures.
 Fix: Use a Core error, add `#Error` to a local error type, or remove the explicit error contract.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.FailureDomainNotErrorType
